From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Oct 2026 01:41:48 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: airoha: npu: add DMA pool memory region

The EN7581 NPU can only address host DRAM at 0x80000000-0xbfffffff;
higher addresses alias the lower 1 GiB. Allow an optional shared DMA
pool, after the firmware region or after the WLAN regions, so coherent
buffers shared with the NPU can be kept inside that window. The
firmware region stays first for existing users.

On 6.18 the binding has not grown the WLAN Block Ack region and the
firmware-name property yet, so describe those here as well; both are
already used by the backported driver patches.

The original version of this patch was written with Codex; it was
rebased onto net-next and its commit message rewritten with Claude
(Anthropic).

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261024154150.45733-2-gilroyscott1970@gmail.com
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/atCRsquzA1UxSpCc@mediatek.com
Signed-off-by: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Chris Scott <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-npu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/airoha,en7581-npu.yaml
@@ -44,18 +44,36 @@ properties:
     oneOf:
       - items:
           - description: NPU firmware binary region
+          - description: Coherent DMA pool for buffers shared with the NPU
+        minItems: 1
       - items:
           - description: NPU firmware binary region
           - description: NPU wlan offload RX buffers region
           - description: NPU wlan offload TX buffers region
           - description: NPU wlan offload TX packet identifiers region
+          - description: NPU wlan Block Ack buffers region
+          - description: Coherent DMA pool for buffers shared with the NPU
+        minItems: 4
 
   memory-region-names:
+    oneOf:
+      - items:
+          - const: firmware
+          - const: dma
+        minItems: 1
+      - items:
+          - const: firmware
+          - const: pkt
+          - const: tx-pkt
+          - const: tx-bufid
+          - const: ba
+          - const: dma
+        minItems: 4
+
+  firmware-name:
     items:
-      - const: firmware
-      - const: pkt
-      - const: tx-pkt
-      - const: tx-bufid
+      - description: Firmware name of RiscV core
+      - description: Firmware name of Data section
 
 required:
   - compatible
